hey guys it's Peter Brown standing in  for freelance reviewer Heidi camps as  the current Naruto manga and anime come  to a close so too does the ultimate  ninja storm game series like its  predecessors ultimate ninja storm 4  features a large roster of characters  from the sprawling saga and offers  stylish battles and free roaming arenas  but for the first time you can assemble  a team of three characters and swap  between them as you bet although they do  share one lifeline ultimate ninja storm  4 is by no means a balanced fighting  game one with layers of esoteric systems  to master but it does have characters  that are simple to control that have  impressive abilities at their disposal  it's easy to become infatuated with the  game's flashy and entertaining battles  for what they are you constantly zip to  and fro while throwing projectiles  executing attack combos and escaping  from danger you can teleport away from  your opponent and attempt a  counter-attack whenever you're under  duress the going gets really tough you  can use items that recover health grant  power boosts or cause massive explosions  since every character has the same basic  control scheme you don't need to worry  about memorizing character specific  command lists ultimate ninja storm 4  isn't well suited for highly competitive  players but it's a great experience for  people who want to experience what it's  like to be a cartoon martial artist with  access to absurdly powerful and  entertaining abilities  developers cyberconnect2 s Naruto games  always receive a great deal of praise  for their visuals an ultimate ninja  storm 4 is no different in this regard  the cel shading on the characters makes  them look almost indistinguishable from  the representation in the anime and  little visual details like armor and  weapons shattering or close  deteriorating from fire elevate the  impressive artwork to new heights when  the game showcases its characters and  elaborately choreographed cutscenes the  visual splendor is even more captivating  but sadly there are less of these scenes  than in the previous Ultimate Ninja  Storm games as some are now presented as  still images instead Ultimate Ninja  Storm 4 is story mode recounts the later  chapters of the Naruto saga taking you  through a chain of interconnected events  and battles from different characters  point of view unfortunately due to its  place in the series timeline anyone who  hasn't followed the show or the manga  will undoubtedly be lost there's also an  adventure mode that offers a series of  fetch quests where your ultimate goal is  to foster a relationship between Naruto  and his blushing bride-to-be Hinata  these quests are definitely basic in  nature but for Naruto fans they're  enjoyable opportunities to wander  through numerous locales from the world  and interact with characters in ways  other than combat but once again the  allure will be lost on anyone who isn't  already a fan of the series rewards that  you earn from the story and adventure  modes can be used to purchase cosmetic  items for characters in your online  profile if you want to get everything  and there's a lot of stuff to get  prepared to spend a lot of time trying  to attain highest ranks and battles and  making sure you satisfy various bonus  conditions of each fight there are the  usual single-player and 2 player free  battles along with online combat free  battle has numerous variations Survival  tournament League and a training focused  practice mode online mode offers limited  time single-player events and rewards  along with online matchmaking oddly  though the online mode in Ultimate Ninja  Storm 4 is missing features from past  games there's no longer a spectator mode  and lobbies are limited to four players  half of what ultimate ninja storm 3  supporting the attention to detail and  ultimate ninja storm 4 will no doubt  please existing fans of Naruto but the  things that group loves may very well  fly over the heads of the  initiated however beneath the fanservice  lies an accessible and entertaining  fighting game that looks great with some  of the best cell shading rendering  around ultimate into storm four can be  enjoyed on a superficial level by all  but it's clearly built for hardcore fans  of the series  you
 

